-- title:
--   Uniform Gotzmann regularity for points of the Hilbert functor
-- statement:
--   Fix $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $P \in \mathbb{Q}[t]$, and assume `hP`: there are a field $K$, an ideal $I \subseteq K[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ stable under taking homogeneous components, and $d_1$ with $\dim_K \bigl(K[x_0,\dots,x_n]_d / I_d\bigr) = P(d)$ for all $d \ge d_1$ (here `piece I d` is the degree-$d$ forms modulo those lying in $I$). Then there is $D_0 \in \mathbb{N}$ such that for every $m \ge D_0$, every field $k$, every scheme $Z_k$ and closed immersion $\iota_k : Z_k \to \operatorname{Proj} k[x_0,\dots,x_n]$, and every point $q$ of the Hilbert functor over $k$ for the numerical function $h =$ `hilbertFunctionOf n P m` (so $q$ consists of an ideal $q.I$ stable under homogeneous components whose graded pieces are finite projective $k$-modules of rank $h(d)$ at every prime, with $h(d) = \binom{n+d}{n}$ for $d < m$ and $h(d) = \lfloor P(d)\rfloor$ otherwise), the following holds. Suppose that for all $d \ge m$ and all forms $F$ of degree $d$, $F \in q.I$ if and only if for every $i$ the pullback along $\iota_k$ of the section $F/x_i^d$ of $\mathcal{O}(d)$ over $D_+(x_i)$ vanishes. Then for every $d \ge m$: (a) for every $i$, the module $\mathrm{HSucc}\,i$ of the twist datum `ProjSpace.twist (ιk ≫ ProjSpace.π k n) ιk d` relative to the pulled-back standard cover of $Z_k$ is a subsingleton, i.e. $\ker d_{i+1}/\operatorname{im} d_i$ vanishes; and (b) every $c$ in the kernel $\mathrm{H0}$ of the zeroth Čech differential for that datum and cover arises from a form: there are $F$ homogeneous of degree $d$ such that for every one-element index $s$ of the cover and every $i \in \{0,\dots,n\}$ the $i$-th component of $c$ at $s$ is the restriction to `inter s ⊓ pullbackChart ιk i` of the pullback along $\iota_k$ of $F/x_i^d$.
--
--   This is Gotzmann's regularity theorem in cohomological form, made uniform in the base field: a single bound $D_0$ depending only on $n$ and $P$ makes the Čech complex of the $d$-th twist on the pulled-back standard cover acyclic in positive degrees and its sections generated by forms of degree $d$, for all $d \ge m \ge D_0$. It feeds the construction of the Hilbert scheme, being cited by [`AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertFunctor.exists_point_I_eq_span_of_isClosedImmersion_of_flat_of_locallyOfFinitePresentation`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertFunctor.exists_point_I_eq_span_of_isClosedImmersion_of_flat_of_locallyOfFinitePresentation).
